    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0516" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg420"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Count
                            Vinci.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 309.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: By a note, dated February 2 last, the royal
                    minister of foreign affairs at Rome advised the embassy of the United States
                    that the minister of commerce had, on January 28 last, issued a circular
                    abolishing the Italian consular visé required for American sanitary certificates
                    accompanying exports of swine flesh to Italy.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose a translation of that note.</p>
                <p>From the inclosed<anchor n="1" xml:id="d353-f1"/> correspondence between the
                    Armour Packing <pb facs="0517" n="421" xml:id="pg421"/> Company and the Italian
                    consular agent at Kansas City, it would seem that the latter had received no
                    instructions in the case, as he still insists that the consular visé must be
                    affixed to the certificate and charges therefor.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to request that you will kindly inquire into the matter and
                    advise the consular officer.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
